  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "It is reported commonly that there is fornication among you, and such fornication as is not so much as named among the Gentiles, that one should have his father’s wife.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And ye are puffed up, and have not rather mourned, that he that hath done this deed might be taken away from among you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For I verily, as absent in body, but present in spirit, have judged already, as though I were present, concerning him that hath so done this deed,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "In the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, when ye are gathered together, and my spirit, with the power of our Lord Jesus Christ,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "To deliver such an one unto Satan for the destruction of the flesh, that the spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Your glorying is not good. Know ye not that a little leaven leaveneth the whole lump?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Purge out therefore the old leaven, that ye may be a new lump, as ye are unleavened. For even Christ our passover is sacrificed for us:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Therefore let us keep the feast, not with old leaven, neither with the leaven of malice and wickedness; but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "I wrote unto you in an epistle not to company with fornicators:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Yet not altogether with the fornicators of this world, or with the covetous, or extortioners, or with idolaters; for then must ye needs go out of the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "But now I have written unto you not to keep company, if any man that is called a brother be a fornicator, or covetous, or an idolater, or a railer, or a drunkard, or an extortioner; with such an one no not to eat.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For what have I to do to judge them also that are without? do not ye judge them that are within?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But them that are without God judgeth. Therefore put away from among yourselves that wicked person.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 5:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:5:13"
      }
    }
  ],
